// Probe 13 — Cluster I LHS border: text concatenation `(a + b) ?? "x"`
//
// Text `+` builds into a function-scope `__work_N` work-buffer (NOT a
// block-local).  If `_ncc_N`'s scope-exit free pattern only fires for
// block-local sources, concat-LHS may ESCAPE the bug — making the
// failure "non-Var LHS *with block-local source*" rather than "any
// non-Var LHS".
//
// If 13 PASSES while 02/04/05 FAIL, the cluster I fix can be narrower:
// only treat block-local-sourced text-coalesces.  If 13 FAILS, the
// non-Var-LHS hypothesis stands — the work-buffer-as-source case has
// its own dangling read.
//
// Pairing: diff against 02 — same `??` consumer, different LHS scope.
// Status: cluster I LHS-border probe.

fn main() {
  a = "pre";
  b = "sent";
  c = (a + b) ?? "fallback";
  assert(c == "present", "probe 13: got '{c}', want 'present'");
  println("probe 13 PASSED");
}
